{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T12:43:16.829Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1699"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1699: secret guard recognises quoted keys, nested JSON values and XML elements"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue 1699 (reported against 2026.11.10): scanMutationSecrets and the CLI mutation guard flag password: value and password=value but miss the same credential when the key is quoted. JSON, Python-dict and XML spellings get no finding, and neither does a credential nested in an array or object under the key. Reproduced on main with the built SDK: {\"password\":\"<8+ chars>\"}, 'password':'<8+ chars>', a nested array, a nested object and <password>...</password> all return []. The high_entropy_assignment rule has the same gap for quoted keys. Root cause: both assignment regexes require the separator to follow the key word directly (\\b(?:password|passphrase)\\s*[:=]), so the key's closing quote defeats them, and neither rule descends into containers. The same SECRET_RULES inventory feeds the repository secret scan (scripts/check-secrets-lib.mjs), so a widened rule must stay clean over all tracked files. Extensions (pm-memory) currently hand-write mixed-content parsers to close these gaps; one structural rule in the SDK replaces them. Duplicate check: searched 'secret guard quoted keys', 'secret', 'credential redact' (open + closed). pm-pim7 (closed) introduced the guard and pm-fhhhlk (closed) added npm/Slack shapes; neither covered key quoting or nesting."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1699","sdk","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-10T12:43:16.829Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T12:43:16.829Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A must-refuse corpus covers the quoted-key (JSON, single-quoted), nested-array, nested-object and XML-element forms from GH-1699 for password_assignment, plus quoted-key high_entropy_assignment; A must-allow corpus keeps \"password\": \"\", \"password\": \"${BUILD_PASSWORD}\", \"password_policy\": \"rotate monthly\", placeholder container tokens such as password=[scrubbed], and prose such as 'the password field' finding-free; The CLI guard (built CLI, real create) and scanMutationSecrets return the same findings for both corpora, and the repository scan reports the same rule for the shared corpus; The structural pass is linear: a pathological input (deep nesting, unterminated strings, many repeated keys) completes within a bounded-time control; node scripts/check-secrets.mjs stays clean over every tracked file"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Quoting the key does not change the result: password_assignment (and high_entropy_assignment) recognise a quoted key followed by a colon, every quoted string nested in an array or object under that key, and <password>...</password> element content, with no new repository-scan findings."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-fhhhlk","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T12:43:16.829Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pim7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-10T12:43:16.829Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"5c87d2721dfd3f6ec57b4877efbfd8360720219e5dc27dfcc3bca1b60d365961","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"48e640f0b676e0995b955f0a281037db21a16e43191d32c605c5a72df1a6c7ef"}
