{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T15:06:46.713Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:06:46.712Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 on PR 1701 (P2): a nested quoted key with a bare value inside a walked container, for example YAML password: {x: 'short', 'password': <value>}, was skipped because the key cursor jumped past the walked container. The key cursor now keeps scanning inside walked containers so nested quoted keys get their scalar check, while a walkedEnd marker ensures each container is still walked only once. Corpus gains the nested YAML and JSON cases. The pathological control still finishes in well under the bound (about 44 ms for the three nested-key inputs), and the fully nested detecting input now yields 2 findings (outer key and innermost quoted scalar)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T15:06:46.713Z"}],"before_hash":"91f18303c3770396f20c0ff3dbfee8f7f47f69f26eaeac7dc6c49f42f329030a","after_hash":"4d8ecbd6638e0cc311f93b22c2d91498e19f3bbada144483235f0f84992d77ab","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c1349e3a6ac49e305e9179138bb5c1581c2c07f4e7b566493933302041ea7d69"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T15:39:54.968Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:39:54.968Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Greptile review on PR 1701 (P1, valid): {\"password\":\"ab\\\\\"cdefghijk\"} produced no finding. The quote-blind value grammar stopped at the escaped quote and saw only 3 characters. Fix: the structured pass now judges a literal containing escapes once more, with each escape sequence counted as one ordinary character (an escape-aware endOfQuoted bounds the literal). This applies to quoted keys, container values and unquoted keys; for unquoted keys only the escaped judgment runs, so a direct match stays the flat rule's single finding. Corpus gains escaped JSON, nested-array and unquoted-key refusals plus a must-allow short value made only of escapes. The repository scan stays clean."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T15:39:54.968Z"}],"before_hash":"4d8ecbd6638e0cc311f93b22c2d91498e19f3bbada144483235f0f84992d77ab","after_hash":"20e8d1c68daa61268456748aedb02372b063df5e69525d26cfcec816949346ad","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d05a20dfe8fe4aec3c067649060b08cc7f1c4bd2fa24a70dc1b8d78033329319"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T16:04:01.522Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:04:01.522Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 on PR 1701, both P2, reproduced and fixed. (a) Escapes: {\"password\":\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\"} was flagged on its raw length, and \\\\u0061\\\\u0062 was mis-measured. A literal containing escapes is now judged only in its decoded length: each complete \\\\uXXXX, \\\\xHH or \\\\X sequence counts as one character. (b) Prefixed keys: {\"reset-password\":\"Reset password\"} was flagged. Each key is now classified as exact (\"password\"), prefixed (\"reset-password\", \"New password\", smtp.password) or malformed (a closing quote with no opening quote within 64 characters on the line, which is skipped). A prefixed key counts only with a whitespace-free value: localization labels are prose, credentials are compact. Exact keys keep passphrases. db_password stays unmatched, as in the flat rule, because no word boundary precedes 'password'. Corpus: +3 refuse, +6 allow; repository scan clean."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T16:04:01.522Z"}],"before_hash":"20e8d1c68daa61268456748aedb02372b063df5e69525d26cfcec816949346ad","after_hash":"b7171e403c891a8fed77766fe965c0408f0cd37a0307401b1e248deb4ddf01b3","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"570e82fbdaaf7412dc88583713cd4d1a7836efe4204f48aa2e7f92d375435e64"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T16:55:24.521Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:55:24.520Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 on PR 1701, both P2, reproduced and fixed. (a) The x-filled escape substitute kept the length but broke the other predicates: 'Reset\\\\u0020password' under a prefixed key was flagged, and a fully \\\\u-escaped high-entropy token lost its entropy. Escaped literals are now decoded faithfully (\\\\uXXXX, \\\\xHH, simple escapes). A decoded quote of the literal's own kind becomes the other quote, and decoded line breaks become spaces, so the grammar's delimiters and raw line-break check still hold. Termination now comes from the escape-aware scanner (scanQuoted), so 'abc\\\\\\\\' closes correctly. (b) An exact nested key's passphrase under a prefixed outer key was lost because the compact walk marked the container as walked. There are now two markers: an exact walk covers everything, while a compact walk covers only prefixed keys. Each character is walked at most twice (60k nested keys in 143 ms)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T16:55:24.521Z"}],"before_hash":"b7171e403c891a8fed77766fe965c0408f0cd37a0307401b1e248deb4ddf01b3","after_hash":"41d201289db288132e094afae2ddd03476c53d80cd27d7b7600c4ca5d1c8cafa","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8da25ccbed425451a9b30303587770e55a0a36b626c24ee4fcb86712b361d376"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T17:55:02.912Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:55:02.911Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 4 on PR 1701 (P2): YAML/Python eight-digit \\\\UXXXXXXXX escapes were consumed as \\\\U plus literal digits. A fully \\\\U-escaped high-entropy token passed, and \\\\U00000061 counted as 9 characters. ESCAPE_SEQUENCE now matches \\\\U followed by 8 hex digits atomically, and the decoder uses String.fromCodePoint, mapping an out-of-range code point to U+FFFD as one opaque character. Specs cover both directions. Follow-up from pm-memory#51 via the fleet session: a literal concatenated with an env reference (password=${EMPTY}\"<literal>\") is skipped by the flat grammar's placeholder lookahead, which is pre-existing behaviour. It is filed as pm-ycgb5g."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T17:55:02.912Z"}],"before_hash":"41d201289db288132e094afae2ddd03476c53d80cd27d7b7600c4ca5d1c8cafa","after_hash":"cd8e2e686a511ccebed1915ee6169f327bf3bfe4ce040b05846ac01980bee4e8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"24acfcceb1f4f41709931a0e08b8ccc9f306007d9a18af67ceee569d307ca9a5"}
