{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T18:43:51.476Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T18:43:51.475Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 5 on PR 1701 (P2): Python octal escapes (\\\\101) were consumed one digit at a time. ESCAPE_SEQUENCE now matches up to three octal digits atomically and decodes them, so \\\\101\\\\102\\\\103 counts as 3 characters (allowed) and an octal-encoded high-entropy token is detected. A bare \\\\0 still decodes to NUL."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T18:43:51.476Z"}],"before_hash":"6f55f3d8b8739ff371607782e872b1e0955faaecc5a04973783127e00cce0871","after_hash":"ea72f1e6df5c97bce11d219ee6367224a0f0efcac60c92ff71d7a9a67bf384fe","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"85f91b8ed0893a42d16d99bfd5f8db38af12713b2f1be4ffdadf6421190781d5"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T19:51:13.533Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T19:51:13.533Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Greptile and CodeRabbit reviews of head 5910631d6. (a) Greptile: TOML and YAML single-quoted strings keep backslashes literally, so decoding '\\\\101\\\\102\\\\103' hid a 12-character password. Double-quoted literals decode in every common format. A single-quoted literal now counts under either its literal or its decoded reading. (b) CodeRabbit: an incomplete \\\\u or \\\\x escape fell through to NUL via parseInt(''). It now decodes to its letter. (c) Element content is documented as judged like an exact key's quoted value (length and placeholder prefix), and the structured-pass docstring now states that each container is walked at most twice."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T19:51:13.533Z"}],"before_hash":"ea72f1e6df5c97bce11d219ee6367224a0f0efcac60c92ff71d7a9a67bf384fe","after_hash":"068f10d8d4a0247a4d3e38ee6d64a6353d377b56de9d9916ae8dc337c0a51ede","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d726549b2fb17a15cec1fcb5dc5c3c6a8679e6183fe25d0b1ed31336b027190f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T23:36:42.079Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-10T23:36:42.078Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 7 on PR 1701 (P2): for a single-quoted literal under a prefixed key, the decoded reading was selected first, and its whitespace (from a decoded \\\\n) failed the compact check before the literal YAML reading was tried. Each reading is now judged independently, and either one qualifying is enough. Spec: \"admin-password\": 'A9b\\\\nC2dE'."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T23:36:42.079Z"}],"before_hash":"068f10d8d4a0247a4d3e38ee6d64a6353d377b56de9d9916ae8dc337c0a51ede","after_hash":"d1a8cafa92afc56ed68b7bb1db2bebd86f58ec95657c51af0e73c64807920605","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"561ba660ec88a8409983fef5d5a8f4b4ed210bb686e6607399b32966a6a197f9"}
